Alembic revisions for the Task Manager API.

Layout
    env.py                  the migration driver (synchronous; see its docstring)
    script.py.mako          the template new revisions are generated from
    versions/0001_baseline.py   the complete schema, with a working downgrade()

There is exactly one revision, and that is deliberate: 0001 creates the whole
schema the domain entities describe. A second revision appears only when a real
change needs one, never as a demonstration that versioning works.

Commands (DATABASE_URL must be set; alembic.ini holds no URL on purpose)

    alembic upgrade head        build the schema
    alembic check               assert the schema matches the ORM models
    alembic downgrade base      remove it again

`alembic check` cannot see CHECK constraints - SQLAlchemy does not reflect them
into a comparable form - so it proves the columns, types, keys and indexes and
nothing about ck_tasks_status and its two siblings. Those are proven by the
integration tests that attempt a forbidden insert and assert the refusal.
